Spec: ServiceDeleteBackupScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  Retire one `ServiceInstance`'s backup machinery from its namespace: run from the install lane's
    backup branch whenever scheduling is OFF — `use_backup` false, no `status.vitals`, or the
    `backup-settings` Secret probe absent-or-erroring (./install.rhai's arms, ./install.sdd branch
    table) — and from the delete lane's `vitals` gate immediately before ./delete_vitals.rhai, this
    file removes the schedule lane's objects by fixed name (CronJob, RoleBinding, ConfigMap) and the
    backup/restore Jobs by label triple, issuing one delete per object and then waiting 300 s each
    for the issued deletions to complete. It is the removal counterpart of ./schedule_backup.rhai:
    the component label its sweep filters on is the one @selector_from_ctx emits into the cron Job
    template (./schedule_backup.sdd). Zero @throw and zero `status` write: every failure inside a
    sweep block is swallowed (`NotFound` on the by-name objects) or @log_warn'ed, and both call
    lanes discard the return whole — a side-effect-only, inventory-free sweeper. Byte-identical
    twin ./../tenant/delete_backup.rhai (diff-verified).

Exposes:
  @run(@instance, @context) — the module's sole @fn and entry point (`delete_backup.rhai` + `run`
    match the entry-point patterns of /agent/src/linting/rhai_checker.sdd); reached ONLY through
    @import_run("delete_backup", instance, context) at three code sites in two shipped lanes:
    ./install.rhai's no-schedule arms (Secret probe failed, and gate-false else) and ./delete.rhai's
    `vitals` gate before `delete_vitals` (./delete.sdd, ./install.sdd freeze the returns as
    discarded whole at every site); no Rust lane names the module — install reaches it inside the
    exit-1 error lane, delete inside the exit-3 one. A package `scripts/delete_backup.rhai`
    shadowing the name replaces the whole lane on the four resolver directories those Rust lanes
    freeze ({package_dir}/scripts winning).

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @ServiceInstance @Dynamic, read for `.metadata.namespace` (the namespace
    argument of all four @k8s_resource constructors and therefore of every touched object) and
    `.metadata.name` (the `app.kubernetes.io/instance` value of both Job selectors) — nothing else;
    `status` is NEVER read: unlike every sibling `delete_*.rhai`, this sweep walks names and labels,
    not the recorded `status` lists.
  @context — the caller-lane map, read ONLY inside guarded zones: `instance.appslug` (the
    CronJob/RoleBinding/ConfigMap name interpolations, CR-side view built by
    ./../lib/build_context.rhai, same value the schedule templates rendered with) and
    `instance["package"].name` (the `app.kubernetes.io/name` selector value, equal by construction to
    the label value @build_context's `selector` carries). Missing map/keys degrade per Handles; the
    rest of the map is hook payload and the returned value.
  Hooks — three optional @import_run module names, each called with the same (instance, context)
    pair: `delete_backup_pre` (outside every try), `delete_backup_prepare` (its raise caught),
    `delete_backup_post` (outside every try, last statement). None ships in any engine directory
    (./, ./../tenant, ./../lib) — package `scripts/` slots only.

Returns:
  The `context` map as held at the end, plus a `delete_backup_post` map-merge — discarded whole by
    all three call sites (./install.sdd, ./delete.sdd freeze the returns as dropped): the lane
    communicates only by deletions it issues and lines it logs. Observable outcome: the named
    CronJob/RoleBinding/ConfigMap in `instance.metadata.namespace` get-deleted when present, every
    Job in that namespace matching either frozen selector get-deleted, then one @log_info +
    @wait_deleted(`60*5` = `300` s) per actually-issued deletion in deletion order.

Raises:
  Zero @throw statement and zero re-`throw` in this file: each sweep block wraps its ENTIRE kind
    work in an @try + @catch pair that finishes the block — @log_warn of the caught string verbatim, or of the
    @json_encode text for non-strings, `_` switch arm of the sibling specs; the three by-name blocks
    additionally swallow any string error containing `NotFound` from the get/delete pair with no log.
  Escape paths to the caller lane: a raise from the `delete_backup_pre` or `delete_backup_post`
    hook (outside every try, so @import_run's two skip markers aside they abort the lane with no log
    here and no marker — the delete lane writes no `set_status_*` at all and this install-lane
    module has none either); a raise from the final wait loop — @wait_deleted timeout or engine
    error on `d` — aborts the remaining waits (their deletions are already issued) with the error
    crossing to install exit-1 or delete exit-3; and @json_encode of an unserializable caught
    payload in a `_` arm can itself raise out of the catch (same open point recorded by
    ./schedule_backup.sdd and ./../lib/backup_context.sdd).
  Import-time failure: the dead top-level import resolving to no module is an eval error before
    @run exists, killing the caller lane (the imported body itself is pure, see Must).

Handles:
  Kind absent from discovery: each block's `api.exist()` false skips that kind ENTIRELY — no log, no
    get/list attempted, no wait record — four independent gates (CronJob, Job, RoleBinding, ConfigMap).
  Never-scheduled instance (the stock path — every stock service install runs this module):
    `get_obj` answers NotFound on all three named kinds, each swallowed silently, the Job selectors
    list empty, the wait loop idle.
  Stock image hooks: all three names take the @import_run skip markers (`No ${name} module, skipping.`
    and `No ${name}::run function, skipping.`, text frozen by ./install.sdd), each return `()` fails
    the `@type_of` == `map` merge guard, lane runs on the untouched context.
  `delete_backup_prepare` raise: warned string-verbatim or through @json_encode, then the sweep
    CONTINUES on the unmerged context — the one hook whose failure this file survives by design.
  Broken context (`()` after a tofu-lane clobber upstream, or missing `instance` sub-keys): the
    name/selector interpolations raise property-on-`()` INSIDE the blocks' try, each block degrades
    to @log_warn and the post hook still runs — the sweep cannot hard-fail on a bad context.
  List race: the Job loops' inner catch keeps NO `NotFound` filter — an object disappearing between
    list and get_obj/delete warns where the by-name blocks stay silent.

Must:
  Execute exactly: @import_run("delete_backup_pre") + map-merge guard → @try {
    @import_run("delete_backup_prepare") + map-merge } + catch-warn → CronJob block → Job block (then
    component `backup` selector loop, then component `restore` selector loop) → RoleBinding block →
    ConfigMap block → for-each over `deleted`: @log_info + @wait_deleted(`60*5`) →
    @import_run("delete_backup_post") + map-merge → return `context`; nothing else, in no other order.
  Sweep exactly these five name/label targets, all scoped to `instance.metadata.namespace` via the
    two-arg namespaced @k8s_resource(kind, ns) constructor:
    by-name @get_obj + @delete — CronJob `${context.instance.appslug}-backups`, RoleBinding
    `${context.instance.appslug}-backups`, ConfigMap `${context.instance.appslug}-backups-scripts`;
    by-label list-then-delete-each over `.items`, each entry re-fetched by @get_obj(`job.metadata.name`)
    before @delete (no collection-delete anywhere) with selector
    `app.kubernetes.io/component=backup,app.kubernetes.io/instance=${instance.metadata.name},app.kubernetes.io/name=${context.instance["package"].name}`
    and the same string with `component=restore` — the exact `instance.selector` + component triple
    @selector_from_ctx emits, so matched Jobs include the cron-spawned backup Jobs, the
    `{appslug}-init-restore` Job from ./init_from.rhai and any manual job carrying the triple, by
    label whatever their names. No other kind is touched: the ServiceAccount the schedule lane
    creates, Roles, PVCs, Secrets and the roleRef ClusterRole are out of this file's inventory.
  Evaluate names and selectors from the CURRENT `context` at block time, so a map merged by
    `delete_backup_prepare` redirects what the sweep deletes.
  Defer all waiting: push each K8sObject whose @delete call returned normally onto `deleted` (objects
    whose delete warned are never pushed nor waited) and wait them AFTER all five sweeps complete, in
    deletion order, one @wait_deleted(`60*5`) each, logging the literal
    `Waiting for ${d.original_kind} ${d.metadata.name} to be deleted` — the @original_kind K8sObject getter, matching the @remove and ./delete_vitals.rhai
    idiom, and the only @log_info lines in the file; @log_warn is the only other log call.
  Load ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai as `dir` at import as the sole top-level statement besides the
    @fn — the imported body is pure fn declarations, so module load itself touches no env, filesystem
    or cluster; `dir` is never invoked (dead import, Tasks).
  Treat success as silence: no `set_status_*` call, condition or tag exists here or is expected from
    the caller's branch (install's close, ./install.sdd's @set_status_ready, is the only status event
    around an install-side sweep).
  Resolve the module and its three hook names against the four resolver directories frozen by the
    install and delete Rust lanes, so packages can ship the hooks or shadow the whole lane.

Must not:
  Sweep from `instance.status` (a status-list walk à la ./delete_vitals.rhai or @remove): presence
    is decided by names, labels and @exist alone, which is what lets an always-installed stock path
    stay silent and lets labels catch Jobs no status ever recorded.
  Apply, create, or re-render anything: schedule objects are only ever removed here — re-scheduling
    is ./schedule_backup.rhai's lane, and pairing this sweep with an @install_obj pass would undo
    the branch gate that invoked it.

Depends on:
  ./../lib/install_from_dir.rhai — imported as `dir`, NEVER called (dead-import Tasks); the
    get-wait-delete/NotFound-swallow idiom it @remove freezes is the shape this file re-implements
    inline (./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd).
  vynil-core 0.7.7 engine API — the @import_run shim (@type_of + skip-marker pair), the
    @k8s_resource(kind, ns) two-arg constructor with @exist + @get_obj + @list (iterating `.items`) and the
    K8sObject @delete + @wait_deleted + @original_kind of the core k8sgeneric registrar (the apiVersion
    constructor and the `k8sworkload`/`k8sraw` surface stay unused here), @type_of, @json_encode;
    @log_warn + @log_info from the core-common helpers. The engine mounts them per
    /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd.
  The three `delete_backup_*` hook names are package-side slots only — no shipped provider.

References:
  ./install.rhai + ./install.sdd — caller half 1: the backup branch table (vitals + `use_backup` +
    `backup-settings` probe) deciding "no schedule → sweep now", return discarded before
    `install_post`.
  ./delete.rhai + ./delete.sdd — caller half 2: `vitals`-directory gate, this module runs FIRST so
    the backup machinery dies before the data stores; return discarded, and a package without
    `vitals/` never sweeps (their Tasks [?]).
  ./schedule_backup.sdd — the creating counterpart: applies ConfigMap `{appslug}-backups-scripts`
    under `has_files`, CronJob `{appslug}-backups`, ServiceAccount and RoleBinding
    `{appslug}-backup` (singular, its naming [?]) whose fact this file settles — see Tasks.
  /agent/templates/cronbackup.yaml.hbs + /agent/templates/init_job.yaml.hbs (+ nested
    backup.yaml.hbs) through @selector_from_ctx /common/src/handlebarshandler.sdd — producers of the
    names and the triple this sweep matches by; @build_context (/agent/scripts/lib/build_context.rhai)
    freezes `appslug`/`selector`/`package.name` value equality between the two sides.
  ./../tenant/delete_backup.rhai — byte-identical twin (diff-verified); ./../tenant/schedule_backup.rhai
    same producer posture.
  /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs — nearest lane test file; no test names this module or its hooks
    (Tasks).

Scenario: stock install without backups sweeps silently
  Given a service install whose backup branch flipped here (no vitals, `use_backup` false, or probe
    failed), no `delete_backup_*` hook on the resolver path, all four kinds discoverable
  When @run executes
  Then all three `get_obj` NotFound answers are swallowed unlogged, both label lists come back
    empty, zero warn/info lines print, the context returns unmerged, and @import_run's caller never
    sees a raise
  No mapped test.

Scenario: disabling a live schedule removes what exists
  Given `instance.appslug` `shop` on a namespace holding CronJob `shop-backups`, ConfigMap
    `shop-backups-scripts`, two Jobs labeled component `backup` and `restore`, plus the
    schedule-applied RoleBinding `shop-backup` and ServiceAccount `shop-backup`
  When @run sweeps
  Then the CronJob, both Jobs and the ConfigMap are get-deleted, the by-name RoleBinding get looks
    for `shop-backups` and swallows its NotFound, and the wait loop logs and @wait_deleted(`60*5`)s
    the four issued deletions in order
  And the RoleBinding `shop-backup` and the ServiceAccount `shop-backup` stay applied — the
    plural/singular seam and missing ServiceAccount sweep are Tasks findings, this Scenario pins
    today's behavior
  No mapped test.

Scenario: delete-lane sweep precedes the vitals teardown
  Given a package with a `vitals/` directory and a CR with backup objects scheduled
  When ./delete.rhai passes its `vitals` gate
  Then @import_run("delete_backup") completes — deletions issued, waits awaited — before
    ./delete_vitals.rhai starts, and its merged-post return reaches no later lane (discarded),
    leaving the ServiceAccount of Scenario 2 alive through the whole instance teardown
  No mapped test.

Scenario: prepare hook failure still sweeps
  Given a package `delete_backup_prepare.rhai` whose run raises the string `prep failed`
  When @run reaches the prepare try
  Then @log_warn prints `prep failed`, `context` keeps the pre-hook value, and all five sweep
    targets are still attempted
  No mapped test.

Scenario: a wait timeout aborts the caller lane late and unrecorded
  Given deletions already issued for three objects and the second @wait_deleted times out
  When the raise leaves the wait loop (outside every try) and crosses @import_run
  Then the third object is never waited, `delete_backup_post` never runs (install side: no
    `install_post`, no close, exit 1; delete side: no `delete_post`, exit 3, no marker anywhere) even
    though its deletion was already issued
  No mapped test.

Scenario: bad context degrades to warned no-ops
  Given `context` reached `()` upstream (tofu-lane clobber frozen in ./install.sdd / ./delete.sdd)
  When @run's blocks interpolate `context.instance.appslug` / `instance["package"].name`
  Then each raise lands in its block's catch and only @log_warn lines print — the sweep never
    deletes a name-resolvable object but the post hook still runs and @run returns without raising
  No mapped test.

Example:
  Swept names: `shop-backups` (CronJob), `shop-backups` (RoleBinding — searched, never matches the
    applied `shop-backup`), `shop-backups-scripts` (ConfigMap)
  Swept Job selector verbatim: `app.kubernetes.io/component=backup,app.kubernetes.io/instance=shop,app.kubernetes.io/name=shop-pkg`
    (second loop identical with `restore`)
  Wait line verbatim pattern: `Waiting for CronJob shop-backups to be deleted`

Tasks:
  [ ] Map the six Scenarios to tests in /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs or a rhai-delete.rs: no test
      names delete_backup, its hooks, or the sweep at all today.
  [ ] Drop or use the dead `import "install_from_dir" as dir;` — mirror of the same open work item
      in ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd Tasks naming both twins.
  [?] RoleBinding/ServiceAccount seam, fact settled / fix open: the producers
      (/agent/templates/cronbackup.yaml.hbs, manualbackup.yaml.hbs, init_job.yaml.hbs) always apply
      SA + RoleBinding `{appslug}-backup` SINGULAR while this file deletes RoleBinding `{appslug}-backups`
      PLURAL (always swallowed) and has no ServiceAccount block at all — so disabling or deleting
      backup leaves both singular objects applied against ClusterRole `{vynil_namespace}:backups`.
      Matches confirmed for CronJob `-backups` and ConfigMap `-backups-scripts`. Decide whether the
      fix pluralizes the two template names or switches this file to singular + adds the
      ServiceAccount sweep (closes the ./schedule_backup.sdd naming [?]).
  [?] Error-posture split inside one file: by-name blocks swallow `NotFound`, Job-loop blocks warn it
      (list/get race noise). Decide one posture.
  [?] `delete_backup_prepare`'s caught-and-continued failure is visible only as a warn line, and
      `delete_backup_pre`/`post` raises abort both caller lanes with no marker anywhere — decide
      whether prepare failures should abort the sweep and whether either pair joins a marker path
      (delete-side has zero `set_status_*` by .sdd freeze).
  [?] Unguarded wait loop: one @wait_deleted timeout strands the rest of `deleted` unwated yet
      deleted and fails the lane (Scenario 5), while @remove in ./../lib/install_from_dir.sdd holds
      the same open shape — decide one posture for both.
  [?] `delete_backup_post` merges its map and it feeds only the discarded return — hooks are
      side-effect-only slots; confirm intended (mirrors ./install.sdd return-discarded open points).

Done when:
  Every Scenario carries a passing mock-engine test or a recorded decision, the sweep inventory,
  selector text and wait posture above still match the source, the naming seam is fixed on whichever
  side Tasks decides, and `specdd lint` is green on this file.
